Robin phone control reuses code from the projects below. The app stays GPL-3.0.

Mobilerun (https://github.com/droidrun/mobilerun)
Copyright (c) 2025 Niels Schmidt
Licensed under the MIT License.
Used for the accessibility-tree index, concise filter, tap-point geometry,
coordinate conversion, and the click / type / swipe / system-button action schema.
MIT text is kept in the headers of the adapted Kotlin files.

mobile-use (https://github.com/minitap-ai/mobile-use)
Copyright 2025 Minitap
Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.
Used for the observe / plan / act / verify loop, element targeting
(resource id, then bounds, then text), and the rule that a goal is complete
only when the next observation shows a change.
http://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0

KeePassDX (https://github.com/Kunzisoft/KeePassDX)
Copyright 2019 Jeremy Jamet / Kunzisoft
Licensed under the GNU General Public License, version 3.
Used for autofill structure parsing: hints, HTML attributes, and Android input
types. Adapted so parsed results keep field ids only and never password values.

Bitwarden Android (https://github.com/bitwarden/android)
Copyright Bitwarden
Licensed under the GNU General Public License, version 3.
Used for the autofill authentication handoff: biometric confirmation before a
fill, and no secret material in model context.

Robin vault records use the existing SecretVault interface (AES-GCM, Android
Keystore). They are not synced to GitHub, Obsidian, or Drive.
